<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.17.4: Transforming the Parent Function</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02052</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.17.4: Transforming the Parent Function</md:title>
    <md:uuid>72f77eb8-48e7-47b6-9fde-6be1b446b0b6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2d08f05ca71c6c6b4e778d6008e158525cddb397"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Do you see two "eyes" and a smiling "mouth" on the graph? The three arcs on the graph all represent quadratic functions that were initially defined by \(y=x^2\), but whose equations were later modified.</para>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Write an equation to represent the smile in the smiley face.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your Answer:</para>
  <para>The mouth can be given by \(y=x^2+10\) because it is the graph of \(y=x^2\)  shifted 10 units upward. </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Write an equation to represent the left eye in the smiley face.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your Answer:</para>
  <para>The left eye can be given by \(y=-(x+2)^2+50\) because the vertex is located at \((-2,50)\) and it opens downward.</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Write an equation to represent the right eye in the smiley face.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your Answer:</para>
  <para>The right eye can be given by \(y=-(x−2)^2+50\) because the vertex is located at \((2,50)\) and it opens downward.</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>What is the domain for the mouth? Write the domain as an inequality.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your Answer:</para>
  <para>For the mouth, the domain is \(-4 \leq x \leq 4\).</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>What is the domain for the left eye? Write the domain as an inequality.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your Answer:</para>
  <para>For the left eye, the domain is \(-3 \leq x \leq -1\) .</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>What is the domain for the right eye? Write the domain as an inequality.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your Answer:</para>
  <para>For the right eye, the domain is \(1 \leq x \leq 3\) .</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
